    The device's default look, without an action bar: an add-on has one
    screen, which draws its own title so that it is laid out with the rest of
    the text rather than above it. DayNight has no NoActionBar variant, hence
    the two items.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.Plugin" parent="@android:style/Theme.DeviceDefault.DayNight">
        <item name="android:windowActionBar">false</item>
        <item name="android:windowNoTitle">true</item>
    </style>
</resources>
